.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_EXCITON "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_exciton (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_exciton \- find ground state of an exciton within a heterostructure.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_exciton
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find exciton binding energy within a heterostructure
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-e\fR [ \fB\-\-dcpermittivity\fR ] arg (=13.18) Bulk relative permittivity
.TP
\fB\-w\fR [ \fB\-\-betastart\fR ] arg (=0.001)
Initial value for beta symmetry
parameter search
.TP
\fB\-x\fR [ \fB\-\-betastep\fR ] arg (=0.05)
Increment for beta symmetry parameter
search
.TP
\fB\-y\fR [ \fB\-\-betastop\fR ] arg (=\-1)
Final value for beta symmetry parameter
search
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [ \fB\-\-lambdastart\fR ] arg (=70)
Initial value for Bohr radius search
[Angstrom]
.TP
\fB\-t\fR [ \fB\-\-lambdastep\fR ] arg (=1)
Increment for beta symmetry parameter
search
.TP
\fB\-u\fR [ \fB\-\-lambdastop\fR ] arg (=\-1)
Final value for beta symmetry parameter
search
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-electronmass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Bulk electron effective mass (relative
to free electron)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR [ \fB\-\-holemass\fR ] arg (=0.62)
Bulk hole effective mass (relative to
free electron)
.TP
\fB\-a\fR [ \fB\-\-electronstate\fR ] arg (=1)
Index of electron state
.TP
\fB\-b\fR [ \fB\-\-holestate\fR ] arg (=1)
Index of hole state
.TP
\fB\-N\fR [ \fB\-\-nx\fR ] arg (=100)
Number of samples for x\-integration
.TP
\fB\-\-searchlogfile\fR arg (=searchlog.r)
Filename for search log
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'wf_ei.r'     Electron wave function amplitude at each position:
   'wf_hi.r'     Hole wave function amplitude at each position:
                 Column 1: position [m]
                 Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

The 'i' is replaced by the number of the state in each subband.

.SS Output files:
   'EX0.r'       Binding energy and symmetry parameters:
                 Column 1: Binding energy [meV].
                 Column 2: Bohr radius [Angstrom].
                 Column 3: Symmetry parameter

   'p.r'         Probability density of carrier separation:
                 Column 1: Carrier separation
                 Column 2: Probability density [1/Angstrom]
   
   'searchlog.r' Log of the search algorithm progress:
                 Column 1: Bohr radius [m]
                 Column 2: Symmetry parameter
                 Column 3: Binding energy [J]
.SH EXAMPLES

Find the exciton binding energy, with the Bohr radius being between 50 and 100 Angstrom:
    qwwad_ef_exciton --lambdastart 50 --lambdastop 100

Find the exciton binding energy for the first electron state and second hole state.
    qwwad_ef_exciton --electronstate 1 --holestate 2
